Client-driven staged job (src/nativeStagedJob.ts): request with a fresh UUID
kept under "erp.cp7.analysis-staged.v1:<scope>", step while RUNNING, back off
and poll get on worker_active, stop on DONE (page set read) or FAILED (code
shown verbatim), resume after reload (get first), abort on unmount without a
timer left behind; strict parser for cp7.native-analysis-staged-job.v1.

Page set / header / page / envelope parsers (src/nativeAnalysisPages.ts)
adapted to §10: no document, no semantic_hash, no source_state; identity_hash
recomputed from header and page sha256 (sha256(header || "\n" || pages...))
and required on every page envelope; header body verified by size and hash;
uneven (byte-adaptive) pages; financial_source must be null. Source check via
erp_cp7_check_staged_analysis_source_v1.

Panel: always-available "Analisis bertahap (hingga 5.000 target)", progress
"Analisis bertahap: tahap i dari n (STAGE) · unit x dari y · dimulai jam …",
"Analisis bertahap dijeda sejak jam …" + "Lanjutkan analisis bertahap",
role=alert with the failure code, finance note, busy signal on "Tutup analisis
bersama"; region "Hasil analisis bertahap" (.native-analysis-staged, run id in
.native-analysis-run span, "N target dalam K halaman.", "Target a–b dari N",
"Halaman sebelumnya/berikutnya", "Cek sumber"); downstream features stated
unavailable. A single capture refused for its target bound releases its
request and offers the staged path; every other single-path behaviour kept.

RPC registrations: erp_cp7_request/step/get_staged_analysis_v1,
erp_cp7_read_staged_analysis_pages_v1, erp_cp7_read_staged_analysis_page_v1,
erp_cp7_check_staged_analysis_source_v1 replace the phase D prototype names in
database.preconnect.ts, check-access-catalog.mjs, check-source-ownership.mjs.

Tests: parser (8), job/driver (8), panel DOM (9), all with real SHA-256.

